# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules for legacy Jekyll URL shapes.
#
# Format: <source>  <destination>  <status>
# Reference: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Audit source: docs/migration/legacy-urls.txt — every REDIRECT row in that
# file MUST appear here, and every rule here MUST trace back to a row in
# that file. The retirement commit (E8) ships this file in the same commit
# as the Jekyll deletions — no window where legacy URLs return 404 (STPA B3).

# --- Canonical legacy post URL ---
/hello-blog/        /posts/hello-blog/     301

# --- Theme taxonomy index pages (no analog on new site) ---
/tags/              /posts/                301
/categories/        /posts/                301

# --- Legacy theme HTML routes ---
/posts.html         /posts/                301
/search.html        /search/               301
/categories.html    /posts/                301
/tags.html          /posts/                301
/index.html         /                      301

# --- Sitemap (legacy single file → Astro sitemap index) ---
/sitemap.xml        /sitemap-index.xml     301
